        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. France: Schoolgirl’s murder sparks outrage over judicial failings Issued on: 08/06/2026 - 17:36 A silent march was held in France on Sunday in memory of an 11-year-old girl whose suspected murder has sparked outrage across the country. The body of the girl, named as Lyhanna, was found last week after she went missing on May 29 near the southwestern town of Fleurance. Anger grew after it emerged that the main suspect had previously been accused of sexually abusing children, but that police had failed to act. 'Once Trump accepted Iranian 14-point proposal as basis of talks, he gave Iran political initiative' 08/06/2026 Middle East French justice system 'overwhelmed': 'Systemic' failures tackling violence against women & children 08/06/2026 France Israel shuts down following war flare-up with Iran 08/06/2026 Middle East Lebanese 'stuck between a rock and a hard place' as Israel strikes south of country 08/06/2026 Middle East Iran halts strikes against Israel, Netanyahu stuck between Trump and ministers 08/06/2026 Middle East Armenian election largely seen as 'national referendum on country's direction' 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific French government 'under pressure' amid public outcry over children protection failures 08/06/2026 France Despite tension over war flare-up, fallout between Trump and Netanyahu unlikely 08/06/2026 Middle East Dissident Chinese artist revisits Monet's waterlilies through Lego art 08/06/2026 Europe"
